Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: retain reclaim progress without blocking Uke presentation

The Uke kernel selects nonblocking GEM reclamation through Rob Clark's
proposed control. Preserve inactive buffer eviction and normal swap; do not
wait on busy buffers while reclaim can hold reservations needed by GPU
retirement. Loaded cover/panel transitions exhibit seconds-long reclaim and
retirement stalls; disabling all eviction isolates the class but is too broad
for a persistent repair. The proposed control provides the narrower policy.

Report actual freed pages even when the scanned LRU becomes empty. The MM
shrinker caller discards SHRINK_STOP before adding progress, so remaining==0
must not discard a successful batch. Preserve STOP when no progress is made.

This kernel is the Uke-specific delivery. The writable control retains its
upstream comparison path without an unversioned module option that would
break older retained kernels. No fence, ownership or busy-buffer safety check
is removed. The original GPL-2.0-only and Rob Clark/Red Hat attribution remains.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(enable_eviction, "Enable swappable GEM buffers");
 module_param(enable_eviction, bool, 0600);
 
-static bool eviction_can_block = true;
+static bool eviction_can_block = false;
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(eviction_can_block, "Enable blocking for GEM buffer to become idle for eviction");
 module_param(eviction_can_block, bool, 0600);
 
@@ -175,7 +175,6 @@
 	};
 	long nr = sc->nr_to_scan;
 	unsigned long freed = 0;
-	unsigned long remaining = 0;
 
 	for (unsigned i = 0; (nr > 0) && (i < ARRAY_SIZE(stages)); i++) {
 		if (!stages[i].cond)
@@ -190,7 +189,6 @@
 					 NULL);
 		nr -= stages[i].freed;
 		freed += stages[i].freed;
-		remaining += stages[i].remaining;
 	}
 
 	if (freed) {
@@ -199,7 +197,7 @@
 				     stages[3].freed);
 	}
 
-	return (freed > 0 && remaining > 0) ? freed : SHRINK_STOP;
+	return freed ? freed : SHRINK_STOP;
 }
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS
